Token.Comment	'-- The "class i wins" idiom, as in examples/acasXu/acasXu.vcl and the mnist-robustness\n'
Token.Comment	'-- specification: a decidable guard `i != j` over a loss-valued comparison. Inverting that\n'
Token.Comment	'-- guard scores the comparison only at `j == i`, where it is trivially satisfied, so the\n'
Token.Comment	'-- loss stops depending on the network at all.\n'
